  "result": "Perfect! All 338 tests pass. I've successfully added foreign currency support to `src/money.js` with comprehensive test coverage.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added foreign currency support to `src/money.js`**:\n\n**RATES constant**: Exchange rates per euro\n- EUR: 1\n- USD: 1.085\n- GBP: 0.8425\n\n**convert(cents, currency)** function:\n- Converts euro cents to another currency's cents\n- Returns `ok(amount_in_cents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n- Example: 100,000 EUR cents \u00d7 1.085 = 108,500 USD cents\n- Handles rounding correctly with banker's rounding\n\n**formatMoney(cents, currency)** function:\n- Formats amounts in a specific currency with proper symbols\n- EUR: \u20ac (euro)\n- USD: $ (dollar)\n- GBP: \u00a3 (pound)\n- Includes thousands separators and 2 decimal places\n- Example: `$1,234.56`, `\u00a30.05`, `-\u20ac10,000.00`\n- Handles unknown currencies by using the currency code\n\n**Added 33 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Exchange rate accuracy\n- Same currency conversion (EUR to EUR)\n- Cross-currency conversion (EUR to USD/GBP)\n- Small and large amounts\n- Zero and negative amounts\n- Precision and rounding\n- Formatting with thousands separators\n- Negative amount formatting with currency symbol placement\n- Unknown currency error handling\n- Case sensitivity of currency codes\n- All supported currencies\n- Rounding consistency\n\nAll 338 tests in the project pass.",
